<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">5 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 5 August, from 1100 to 1962.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/england" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1100 CE <span class="tih-ago">926 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry I is crowned King of England</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Three days after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-ii-of-england">William Rufus</a> died in a hunting accident, his brother Henry was crowned at Westminster. His Charter of Liberties and administrative reforms made him one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>'s ablest medieval kings.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1583 CE <span class="tih-ago">443 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sir Humphrey Gilbert claims Newfoundland for England</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At St John's harbour, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humphrey-gilbert">Humphrey Gilbert</a> claimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a>, an early step in English overseas expansion. No settlement followed, and Gilbert was lost at sea on the voyage home.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humphrey-gilbert">Humphrey Gilbert</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1858 CE <span class="tih-ago">168 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The first transatlantic telegraph cable is completed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Cable ships landed the ends of the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telegraph">telegraph</a> line across the Atlantic in Ireland and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a>. It carried messages for just three weeks before failing, but proved the idea possible.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1884 CE <span class="tih-ago">142 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cornerstone laid for the Statue of Liberty's pedestal</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The cornerstone of the pedestal was laid on Bedloe's Island in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> Harbor. Americans had to raise the funds for the base, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> paid for the statue itself.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1914 CE <span class="tih-ago">112 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">An electric traffic signal is installed in Cleveland</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An electric traffic signal with red and green lights was installed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euclid">Euclid</a> Avenue and East 105th Street in Cleveland, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohio">Ohio</a>. It is often cited as the first of its kind in the world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euclid">Euclid</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1962 CE <span class="tih-ago">64 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Marilyn Monroe is found dead in Los Angeles</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Marilyn Monroe was found dead at her home in Brentwood, aged 36; the coroner ruled probable suicide from barbiturates. Her death cut short the career of Hollywood's most famous star.</p></div></li></ol>
